**Medium Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
`PrepareTranscript` short-circuits with a no-op when the file already exists, but for resumed sessions (turn 2+), the file persists from the previous turn-end's `fetchAndCacheExport` call and contains stale data. Since `GetTranscriptPosition` reads from this stale file, `currentPos` equals `CheckpointTranscriptStart` (both derived from the same old data), causing the "no new content" check to pass and no checkpoint to be created. Unlike `fetchAndCacheExport` (used at turn-end) which always calls `opencode export` and overwrites, `PrepareTranscript` never refreshes an existing file — so mid-turn commits in turn 2+ still won't produce checkpoints.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

